      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "The base rate is the six consecutive original first prints for March-August 2026. Their mean is 7.297833 million. August's 7.079 million anchors persistence, while the May-August decline of 0.515 million supplies a modest negative momentum update. Original-vintage observations also determine dispersion."
      },
      {
        "kind": "tool",
        "tool": "official.lookup",
        "call": "Open https://www.bls.gov/news.release/jolts.t01.htm and read the seasonally adjusted total and industry rows.",
        "result": "August 2026 openings were 7079 thousand, versus revised July's 7335 thousand, a decrease of 256 thousand. Professional and business services decreased 119 thousand; health care and social assistance decreased 115 thousand; leisure and hospitality increased 61 thousand."
      },
      {
        "kind": "tool",
        "tool": "official.lookup",
        "call": "Open https://www.bls.gov/news.release/empsit.nr0.htm, the September 2026 Employment Situation released October 2.",
