      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Level and momentum are modeled separately. September's weak payroll growth corroborates subdued recruiting, supporting the damped negative momentum term. One-off and policy-mechanism adjustments are each zero because the fetched evidence supplies no quantified October effect. The shrinkage coefficients below are judgmental model choices."
      },
      {
        "kind": "math",
        "text": "Prior/update/interval: Use August persistence plus 25% reversion toward the six-print mean and 25% extrapolation of recent momentum over two months. Level = 7.079; reversion = 0.25*(7.297833-7.079) = +0.054708; momentum = 0.25*2*(7.079-7.594)/3 = -0.085833; one-off = 0; policy = 0. Point = 7.047875, rounded to 7.048 million. The five successive original-print changes are 0.752, -0.024, -0.235, -0.088, and -0.192 million, with mean 0.0426. Sample sigma = 0.405228 million = sqrt(0.6568392/4). The one-month 80% half-width is 1.28*sigma = 0.518692. Allowing two monthly innovations gives half-width = 1.28*0.405228*sqrt(2) = 0.733541. Bounds = 7.047875 +/- 0.733541 = [6.314334, 7.781416], rounded to [6.314, 7.781]. This approximate Gaussian interval assumes independent monthly innovations; six original prints provide limited calibration."
      },
